WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.296 --> 00:00:07.619
"Who will be my valentine?"

2
00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:08.879
Caroline wondered.

3
00:00:09.399 --> 00:00:13.481
She needed to choose soon—Valentine's Day was the next day!

4
00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:18.183
"Maybe I should choose Tommy," she thought.

5
00:00:18.203 --> 00:00:21.885
"Or perhaps I should choose Tyler!"

6
00:00:21.905 --> 00:00:25.146
"Put your books away.

7
00:00:25.426 --> 00:00:29.107
It's time for art," Miss Smith said to the whole class.

8
00:00:29.508 --> 00:00:32.834
"Today we are making Valentine's cards."

9
00:00:33.935 --> 00:00:37.838
"Tommy or Tyler, who will it be," wondered Caroline.

10
00:00:37.858 --> 00:00:44.003
"Maybe if I cut out a big red heart, my heart will help me choose."

11
00:00:45.965 --> 00:00:48.287
Caroline cut out a red paper heart.

12
00:00:49.328 --> 00:00:52.491
When she finished, the heart began to hum.

13
00:00:55.393 --> 00:01:01.281
Then, it jumped up and began to sing, "I am your Valentine's heart.

14
00:01:02.141 --> 00:01:03.441
I am really smart!

15
00:01:04.141 --> 00:01:06.722
Write a poem to the one you love the best.

16
00:01:07.282 --> 00:01:10.443
And I will sing, dance, and do the rest!"

17
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:12.944
Caroline wrote her poem.

18
00:01:13.504 --> 00:01:19.405
It was lovely and sweet, but she still didn't know who to give her Valentine's Day heart to.

19
00:01:20.986 --> 00:01:25.227
Caroline added white lace and a small red bow to her heart.

20
00:01:26.527 --> 00:01:33.359
Her heart looked pretty, but still she wondered, "Tommy or Tyler, who should I choose?

21
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.842
Who will receive my Valentine's Day heart?"

22
00:01:38.804 --> 00:01:42.567
The next day was Valentine's Day—February 14!

23
00:01:43.347 --> 00:01:45.989
The classroom was decorated in pink and white.

24
00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.251
The children giggled happily.

25
00:01:48.271 --> 00:01:55.017
"Now it is time to give your Valentine's heart away," said Miss Smith.

26
00:01:55.937 --> 00:01:58.760
Miss. Smith had hung a red curtain in the classroom.

27
00:01:59.496 --> 00:02:01.618
She separated the boys and girls.

28
00:02:02.499 --> 00:02:05.021
Each stood on a different side of the curtain.

29
00:02:05.682 --> 00:02:09.825
Caroline's heart beat as she stepped to her side of the curtain.

30
00:02:10.906 --> 00:02:13.388
She still had not chosen her valentine.

31
00:02:14.109 --> 00:02:19.494
Then to her surprise, her Valentine's Day heart began to spell out a name.

32
00:02:20.094 --> 00:02:24.438
Letters appeared on her heart and spelled out "T–y–l–e–r."

33
00:02:27.352 --> 00:02:31.995
"Tyler! Come and be my Valentine," called Caroline.

34
00:02:33.096 --> 00:02:35.478
Tyler sprang from behind the red curtain.

35
00:02:36.058 --> 00:02:39.361
Caroline gave him a hug and her Valentine's Day heart.

36
00:02:40.261 --> 00:02:42.863
All day Caroline and Tyler sat together.

37
00:02:43.704 --> 00:02:47.026
At recess Tyler pushed Caroline on the swing.

38
00:02:48.527 --> 00:02:57.942
And the Valentine's Day heart sang, "Valentine's Day, Valentine's Day, what a happy day to play!

39
00:02:58.582 --> 00:03:04.847
I really hope to hear you say, 'I love you,' on this happy Valentine's Day!"
